WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.062
Muhammad Ali by Bernard Smith, level one.

00:00:05.122 --> 00:00:07.984
Who is Muhammad Ali?

00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:10.844
Why is he famous?

00:00:10.904 --> 00:00:19.679
Why did he have two names, Cassius Clay, in his early years, and later Muhammad Ali?

00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:22.920
And what is he doing now?

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:30.682
Muhammad Ali was, of course, a famous boxer, a world champion.

00:00:30.742 --> 00:00:34.452
But he fought for black Americans too.

00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:40.446
He stopped boxing in 1981 because he was sick.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:45.718
But today he is fighting for peace in the world.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:55.464
The Red and White Bike The story starts with a boy's new red and white bike.

00:00:55.524 --> 00:00:58.088
It is 1954.

00:00:58.148 --> 00:01:07.739
Joe Martin is a policeman in Louisville, Kentucky, but he teaches boxing in a gym in the evenings, too.

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:12.594
One day, two young black boys come into the gym.

00:01:12.654 --> 00:01:15.436
One of them sees Joe.

00:01:15.496 --> 00:01:17.498
Excuse me?

00:01:17.557 --> 00:01:23.002
He says, are you Joe Martin, the policeman?

00:01:23.062 --> 00:01:24.684
That's right.

00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:28.499
Joe says, what's your problem?

00:01:28.559 --> 00:01:32.453
It's my new back," the boy says.

00:01:32.513 --> 00:01:34.894
It's red and white.

00:01:34.954 --> 00:01:39.856
He was in front of this building and now it's not there.

00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:45.318
The young boy is unhappy and very angry.

00:01:45.378 --> 00:01:49.119
I'm going to find the boy with my back.

00:01:49.179 --> 00:01:52.450
Then I'm going to whoop him.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:56.011
He says again and again.

00:01:56.071 --> 00:01:58.675
Joe Martin smiles.

00:01:58.735 --> 00:02:01.650
The boy is about twelve years old.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:06.444
He is tall with long legs, and he is thin.

00:02:06.504 --> 00:02:08.906
Can you box?

00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:10.828
Joe asks.

00:02:10.887 --> 00:02:13.790
No, I can't box.

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.452
The boy says.

00:02:15.511 --> 00:02:18.524
But I want to whoop that boy.

00:02:18.584 --> 00:02:21.516
Joe smiles again.

00:02:21.576 --> 00:02:24.688
Come here to the gym first.

00:02:24.748 --> 00:02:27.441
Maybe I can teach you.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.212
Okay.

00:02:29.272 --> 00:02:33.384
The boy says, I'd like that.

00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:36.776
Good, Joe says.

00:02:36.836 --> 00:02:39.158
What's your name?

00:02:39.218 --> 00:02:45.482
Cassius, the boy says, Cassius Clay.

00:02:45.542 --> 00:02:55.998
Joe doesn't know it, but in only 10 years, that young black boy is going to be a world boxing champion.

00:02:56.058 --> 00:03:02.936
After that, Cassius went to Joe Martin's gym six days a week.

00:03:02.996 --> 00:03:11.317
He was strong and quick on his feet, and he started boxing with the other boys in the gym.

00:03:11.377 --> 00:03:15.058
He didn't box for money, of course.

00:03:15.118 --> 00:03:18.818
He boxed because he liked it.

00:03:18.878 --> 00:03:21.919
He usually won his fights.

00:03:21.979 --> 00:03:28.866
He was good, but he wasn't a good student at school.

00:03:28.926 --> 00:03:32.025
He had a lot of problems.

00:03:32.084 --> 00:03:35.956
He was a good boy from a good family.

00:03:36.016 --> 00:03:40.338
He was friendly and his teachers liked him.

00:03:40.398 --> 00:03:44.982
But schoolwork was very difficult for him.

00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:52.215
The only important thing in the world for him, then, was boxing.

00:03:52.275 --> 00:03:57.084
In six years, he had 108 fights.

00:03:57.144 --> 00:04:00.990
and he won 100 of them.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:10.612
Then, in 1960, he went to Rome and box for the United States.

00:04:10.672 --> 00:04:22.364
The Olympic Games In 1960, Cassius was only 18 years old.

00:04:22.424 --> 00:04:33.276
He was in Rome for the Olympic Games He beat every opponent, and he won an Olympic medal for the United States.

00:04:33.336 --> 00:04:44.446
He was an Olympic boxing champion, and he didn't take off his Olympic medal for weeks, night or day.

00:04:44.506 --> 00:05:01.340
At home in Louisville, he was famous, but he was black And in Louisville in the 1960s, there were places for white people and places for black people.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:12.146
In many hotels, theaters, stores, and buses, black people didn't sit with white people.

00:05:12.206 --> 00:05:18.381
One day, Cassius wanted to buy a drink in a white store.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.109
It was a problem.

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:25.538
Whites only, they said.

00:05:25.597 --> 00:05:29.150
But I'm the Olympic boxing champion.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.102
I'm famous, Cassius said.

00:05:33.162 --> 00:05:36.694
Whites only, they answered.

00:05:36.754 --> 00:05:39.186
Go away.

00:05:39.246 --> 00:05:43.898
Cassius was very unhappy about that.

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:48.944
I'm going to be the world champion, he said.

00:05:49.004 --> 00:05:58.266
I'm going to be important, then why people are going to sit down with me and listen to me."

00:05:58.326 --> 00:06:04.500
After the Olympic Games, Cassius started to fight for money.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.513
Boxing wasn't a game now.

00:06:08.572 --> 00:06:11.255
It was his work.

00:06:11.315 --> 00:06:15.168
He moved from Louisville to Miami.

00:06:15.227 --> 00:06:18.152
He went to a new gym in Miami.

00:06:18.212 --> 00:06:20.894
and he had new friends.

00:06:20.954 --> 00:06:25.166
One of them was Angelo Dundee.

00:06:25.226 --> 00:06:33.329
He worked with Cassius in the gym and was always with him for his fights.

00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:39.982
The first fight with Sonny Liston.

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:45.848
In 1964, Cassius Clay was 22 years old.

00:06:45.908 --> 00:06:50.754
He was tall and strong.

00:06:50.814 --> 00:07:00.996
After 19 fights and 19 wins, he wanted to fight the world champion, Sonny Liston.

00:07:01.056 --> 00:07:05.888
Clay always moved very quickly in his fights.

00:07:05.948 --> 00:07:10.469
He danced here and there in the ring.

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:15.050
His opponents were big, strong men.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:22.054
but they lost because their punches usually didn't hit him.

00:07:22.114 --> 00:07:29.729
But Liston was the world champion and a very strong boxer.

00:07:29.789 --> 00:07:37.034
The newspapers in the US said, Liston is going to win this fight.

00:07:37.094 --> 00:07:40.126
Clay is very young.

00:07:40.186 --> 00:07:44.346
Liston is going to kill him.

00:07:44.406 --> 00:07:53.468
Only three newspapers said, maybe Clay can beat the champion.

00:07:53.528 --> 00:08:02.192
The fight was in Miami and it was on television in a lot of American theaters too.

00:08:02.252 --> 00:08:08.856
Young Cassius Clay wanted to be famous and make a lot of money.

00:08:08.915 --> 00:08:13.648
Before his fights, he played a game.

00:08:13.708 --> 00:08:15.461
He talked.

00:08:15.521 --> 00:08:17.455
and talked.

00:08:17.515 --> 00:08:25.983
Usually boxers were quiet men, but Clay's mouth was always open.

00:08:26.043 --> 00:08:35.222
Before every fight he said to the people and the newspapers, I'm beautiful.

00:08:35.282 --> 00:08:37.304
I'm good.

00:08:37.364 --> 00:08:40.506
I'm quick and strong.

00:08:40.566 --> 00:08:48.671
I'm going to beat that man in two or three or four rounds.

00:08:48.731 --> 00:08:52.623
White people were angry with him.

00:08:52.683 --> 00:08:58.016
They didn't like this young black man with the big mouth.

00:08:58.076 --> 00:09:03.470
Kill him, they said to his opponents.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:07.752
Close that big mouth for him.

00:09:07.812 --> 00:09:14.880
But then, of course, A lot of people wanted to see the fight.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:21.616
Before the fight with Sonny Liston, Clay played this same game.

00:09:21.676 --> 00:09:28.941
Liston was very strong, but he wasn't very quick.

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:33.705
The fight is on February 25th.

00:09:33.765 --> 00:09:38.419
In round one, Clay starts to dance.

00:09:38.479 --> 00:09:41.871
Liston can't hit him.

00:09:41.931 --> 00:09:46.344
Sometimes Clay hits his opponent's face.

00:09:46.404 --> 00:09:50.537
One, two, very quick punches.

00:09:50.597 --> 00:09:54.200
Then he moves away.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:59.634
Listen goes after him, but slowly.

00:09:59.694 --> 00:10:07.110
He is big and strong, but he can't hit the young Clay.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:10.967
Clay goes back to his chair.

00:10:11.027 --> 00:10:16.503
He smiles at his friend, Angelo Dundee.

00:10:16.563 --> 00:10:23.084
That's the first round, and he didn't kill me, he says.

00:10:23.144 --> 00:10:25.815
I can win this.

00:10:25.875 --> 00:10:29.296
Liston is on his feet.

00:10:29.356 --> 00:10:32.426
He doesn't want to sit down.

00:10:32.486 --> 00:10:36.352
He wants to start round two.

00:10:36.412 --> 00:10:44.169
But it is the same story in rounds two, and three, and four.

00:10:44.229 --> 00:10:50.810
Clay dances across the ring, and Liston can't catch him.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:11:05.815
Sometimes he hits Clay, of course, but Clay is always moving away, and he is hitting Liston's face and eyes all the time.

00:11:05.874 --> 00:11:11.288
After six rounds, Liston sits down.

00:11:11.348 --> 00:11:16.379
His face is red, and one eye is closing.

00:11:16.439 --> 00:11:20.460
Suddenly, he is very tired.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:25.882
That man can hit, he says.

00:11:25.942 --> 00:11:32.674
Now it is round seven, and Clay is standing up on his feet.

00:11:32.734 --> 00:11:34.828
He is waiting.

00:11:34.888 --> 00:11:38.823
but his opponent isn't moving from his chair.

00:11:38.883 --> 00:11:48.776
Cassius Clay is the new champion of the world, and he is only 22 years old.

00:11:48.836 --> 00:11:53.572
He calls to the newspaperman near the ring.

00:11:53.632 --> 00:11:55.917
I am the champion.

00:11:55.937 --> 00:11:58.058
I'm beautiful.

00:11:58.078 --> 00:12:01.419
I'm number one in the world.

00:12:01.479 --> 00:12:06.600
And you were all wrong, wrong, wrong.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:15.773
A new name and new problems.

00:12:15.833 --> 00:12:24.190
The day after that first fight with Liston, Cassius Clay had a new name.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:30.278
My name is not Cassius Clay now," he said.

00:12:30.338 --> 00:12:34.740
It's Muhammad Ali.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.821
Ali's family was unhappy about this.

00:12:39.881 --> 00:12:47.644
His father, Cass Clay, and his mother were good Christian people.

00:12:47.704 --> 00:12:53.176
Their two sons were always good Christians too.

00:12:53.236 --> 00:12:59.538
They loved their mother and father and had a happy home.

00:12:59.598 --> 00:13:03.799
What's wrong with the name Clay?

00:13:03.859 --> 00:13:06.120
His father asked.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:08.280
It's a good name.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.902
It's our name.

00:13:10.962 --> 00:13:16.963
Clay is a white man's name, Ali said.

00:13:17.023 --> 00:13:24.438
We have that name because our family worked for Mr. Clay, a white man.

00:13:24.498 --> 00:13:31.782
Our family came from Africa and I would like a new name, a black name.

00:13:31.842 --> 00:13:37.926
And from today, I'm going to be a Muslim because in the U.S.

00:13:37.986 --> 00:13:40.518
white people are Christians.

00:13:40.578 --> 00:13:48.037
My black brothers are Muslims and I'm going to be a Muslim too.

00:13:48.097 --> 00:13:55.034
Later that year Ali visited Egypt and Africa.

00:13:55.094 --> 00:13:58.186
He talked to Muslims there.

00:13:58.246 --> 00:14:02.567
There are Muslims of all colors in the world.

00:14:02.627 --> 00:14:05.488
He said, I know that now.

00:14:05.508 --> 00:14:12.750
Our problem in the US is only with the bad white people there.

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:19.556
But he liked his new Muslim name and he stayed in Muslim.

00:14:19.616 --> 00:14:25.711
Fifteen months later, he and Sonny Liston fought again.

00:14:25.771 --> 00:14:33.912
This time, Liston was on his face on the floor in the first round.

00:14:33.972 --> 00:14:40.414
Muhammad Ali was the world boxing champion.

00:14:40.474 --> 00:14:42.774
In 1967, the U.S.

00:14:42.834 --> 00:14:46.034
Army was in Vietnam.

00:14:46.094 --> 00:14:54.879
thousands of young Americans, white and black, went into the U.S.

00:14:54.939 --> 00:14:58.532
Army and fought the Viet Cong.

00:14:58.592 --> 00:15:00.074
The U.S.

00:15:00.134 --> 00:15:07.690
government called Muhammad Ali and said, Your country wants you in the army.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:12.074
You have to go to Vietnam.

00:15:12.134 --> 00:15:18.946
Ali answered, I'm a Muslim and Muslims want peace.

00:15:19.006 --> 00:15:21.868
They don't fight and kill people.

00:15:21.928 --> 00:15:24.269
Who are the Vietcong?

00:15:24.329 --> 00:15:28.311
They don't want to kill me and I don't want to kill them.

00:15:28.331 --> 00:15:32.882
I'm not going to go into the army.

00:15:32.942 --> 00:15:36.974
This was a big problem.

00:15:37.034 --> 00:15:46.004
The US government said, go into the army or go to jail.

00:15:46.064 --> 00:15:54.436
The American people were angry with Ali, and they really didn't like him.

00:15:54.496 --> 00:15:58.328
You can't box in the US.

00:15:58.388 --> 00:16:03.922
You can't be world champion, the government said.

00:16:03.982 --> 00:16:09.496
And you can't go and box in other countries.

00:16:09.556 --> 00:16:14.149
But Ali didn't go into the army.

00:16:14.209 --> 00:16:17.044
I'm a boxer.

00:16:17.104 --> 00:16:23.831
He said, I fight people because that's my job.

00:16:23.891 --> 00:16:27.913
But I don't kill people.

00:16:27.973 --> 00:16:32.676
Ali didn't box for two years.

00:16:32.736 --> 00:16:38.448
He talked to students in schools and got a little money.

00:16:38.508 --> 00:16:42.925
He talked about peace in Vietnam.

00:16:42.985 --> 00:16:51.002
The fighting in Vietnam is wrong, he always said.

00:16:51.062 --> 00:16:58.744
The government didn't send him to jail, but he didn't have much money.

00:16:58.804 --> 00:17:08.296
Then in 1970, the US government said, you can box again.

00:17:08.357 --> 00:17:13.185
But there was a new world champion now.

00:17:13.246 --> 00:17:17.264
Joe Frazier.

00:17:17.324 --> 00:17:23.406
Joe Frazier a new opponent.

00:17:23.466 --> 00:17:28.138
Joe Frazier was a good boxer.

00:17:28.198 --> 00:17:31.540
He was strong and quick.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:35.442
He was an Olympic champion too.

00:17:35.502 --> 00:17:42.045
He won his medal at the Olympic Games in Tokyo in 1964.

00:17:42.105 --> 00:17:56.216
Ali's first fight with him was in New York in 1971, but two years away from boxing is a long time.

00:17:56.276 --> 00:18:00.880
The fight was very difficult for Ali.

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:06.764
He danced, but he was slow and tired.

00:18:06.825 --> 00:18:15.004
He fought well but after 15 long rounds, Frazier won.

00:18:15.064 --> 00:18:19.746
But Ali didn't stop fighting.

00:18:19.806 --> 00:18:30.903
After 13 fights and 12 wins, he fought Joe Frazier again in New York in 1974.

00:18:30.963 --> 00:18:43.972
Frazier fought well, but after a long and difficult fight, This time, Ali was the winner.

00:18:44.032 --> 00:18:49.526
But Ali wasn't the world champion after that fight.

00:18:49.586 --> 00:18:56.779
At that time, there was a new world champion, George Foreman.

00:18:56.838 --> 00:19:03.922
I want to be world champion again, Ali said.

00:19:03.982 --> 00:19:08.968
And only George Foreman can stop me now.

00:19:09.028 --> 00:19:14.525
When and where can I fight him?

00:19:14.585 --> 00:19:21.651
Ali and Foreman, the big fight.

00:19:21.711 --> 00:19:27.396
The Ali Foreman fight wasn't in the US.

00:19:27.456 --> 00:19:32.010
It was in Kinshasa in Zaire.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:35.902
Ali loved Africa.

00:19:35.962 --> 00:19:39.706
Zaire was a black country.

00:19:39.766 --> 00:19:43.348
The government was black.

00:19:43.408 --> 00:19:51.563
Ali stayed in a beautiful big hotel, and the people there loved him.

00:19:51.623 --> 00:20:00.028
He was on the streets of Kinshasa every day, and people called to him.

00:20:00.087 --> 00:20:01.038
Ali!

00:20:01.058 --> 00:20:01.678
Bama-ye!

00:20:01.698 --> 00:20:01.979
Ali!

00:20:02.039 --> 00:20:03.019
Bama-ye!

00:20:03.039 --> 00:20:07.017
Bama-ye!

00:20:07.077 --> 00:20:12.666
What are they saying?

00:20:12.726 --> 00:20:15.778
Ali asked a man.

00:20:15.838 --> 00:20:19.310
The man had a big smile.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:24.594
They're saying Ali kill him.

00:20:24.654 --> 00:20:30.496
Of course, George Foreman was a black American too.

00:20:30.557 --> 00:20:38.052
But Africans loved Ali because he wanted peace in Vietnam.

00:20:38.112 --> 00:20:44.833
And he was very famous because he didn't go into the US Army.

00:20:44.893 --> 00:20:51.534
But George Foreman was a very big, strong boxer.

00:20:51.594 --> 00:20:58.076
He was 25 years old, and Ali was 32.

00:20:58.136 --> 00:21:02.716
And Foreman wasn't slow and heavy.

00:21:02.776 --> 00:21:15.913
At 4 o'clock on the morning of October 30, 1974, Ali and Foreman start the big fight.

00:21:15.973 --> 00:21:20.306
It is very hot in Kinshasa.

00:21:20.366 --> 00:21:24.828
There is going to be heavy rain later in the day.

00:21:24.888 --> 00:21:32.342
In round one Ali starts to move and dance across the ring.

00:21:32.403 --> 00:21:35.984
Foreman comes after him.

00:21:36.044 --> 00:21:41.183
In the first round there is no winner.

00:21:41.244 --> 00:21:44.922
Ali sits down.

00:21:44.982 --> 00:21:50.736
I can't dance for 15 rounds, he thinks.

00:21:50.797 --> 00:21:55.110
It's very hot and forming is quick.

00:21:55.170 --> 00:22:00.164
The old game isn't going to work.

00:22:00.224 --> 00:22:05.638
In round two, Ali stops dancing.

00:22:05.698 --> 00:22:09.178
He tries a new game.

00:22:09.238 --> 00:22:13.758
He is going to make his opponent tired.

00:22:13.818 --> 00:22:16.460
He moves slowly.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.532
Sometimes, he only stands there.

00:22:20.592 --> 00:22:25.984
Foreman hits him with big, heavy punches.

00:22:26.044 --> 00:22:28.436
People call out.

00:22:28.496 --> 00:22:30.847
Dance Ali!

00:22:30.907 --> 00:22:32.438
Dance!

00:22:32.498 --> 00:22:34.379
Don't stop moving!

00:22:34.399 --> 00:22:38.189
He's killing you!

00:22:38.249 --> 00:22:46.504
For six rounds, Foreman hits Ali again and again.

00:22:46.564 --> 00:22:50.717
But Ali stays on his feet.

00:22:50.777 --> 00:22:56.662
In round eight, Foreman is getting slow.

00:22:56.722 --> 00:23:00.334
He is very hot and tired.

00:23:00.394 --> 00:23:04.808
His hands are heavy and slow.

00:23:04.868 --> 00:23:08.931
Suddenly, Ali is quick.

00:23:08.991 --> 00:23:11.423
and strong again.

00:23:11.483 --> 00:23:20.550
He hits his opponent again and again, and suddenly Foreman is on the floor.

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:23.412
He can't stand up.

00:23:23.472 --> 00:23:28.156
Ali is dancing.

00:23:28.176 --> 00:23:33.050
He is the world champion again.

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:38.852
Ali stayed the champion for six years.

00:23:38.912 --> 00:23:50.643
He beat Joe Frazier again in Manila in 1975 after a long and difficult fight.

00:23:50.703 --> 00:23:57.635
In 1978, Ali lost a fight with Leon Spinks in Las Vegas.

00:23:57.695 --> 00:24:12.321
But then, seven months later, he beat him Ali was the new world champion three times in 14 years.

00:24:12.381 --> 00:24:19.825
A quiet time with his family.

00:24:19.885 --> 00:24:24.658
In 1980, Ali lost a fight with Larry Holmes.

00:24:24.718 --> 00:24:29.212
And in 1981, he lost again to Trevor Burbank.

00:24:29.272 --> 00:24:34.690
He was slow and tired.

00:24:34.750 --> 00:24:40.063
He wasn't well, and he went to a doctor.

00:24:40.123 --> 00:24:45.917
You're very sick, the doctor said.

00:24:45.977 --> 00:24:49.380
And you're not going to get well.

00:24:49.440 --> 00:24:58.836
It's not going to kill you, but you're going to get tired very quickly, every day.

00:24:58.896 --> 00:25:04.380
You're going to walk slowly and talk slowly.

00:25:04.440 --> 00:25:09.442
I'm sorry, but we can't stop it.

00:25:09.502 --> 00:25:15.676
And, of course, you can't box.

00:25:15.736 --> 00:25:20.038
Ali stopped boxing.

00:25:20.098 --> 00:25:28.849
Now he lives quietly with his family in a big house in the country in Michigan.

00:25:28.909 --> 00:25:35.842
In the US today, there are no places for whites only.

00:25:35.902 --> 00:25:43.158
On television and in movies, there are faces of all colors.

00:25:43.218 --> 00:25:47.172
People are people.

00:25:47.232 --> 00:26:02.098
Ali is happy because he was one of the first famous black Americans and now Ali is working for peace in the world.

00:26:02.158 --> 00:26:06.270
He makes money with his famous name.

00:26:06.330 --> 00:26:11.924
He meets and talks with governments and other famous people.

00:26:11.984 --> 00:26:15.796
He gets medals these days too.

00:26:15.856 --> 00:26:30.685
He is a worker for peace in the world, peace for all people, blacks and whites Christians and Muslims.

00:26:30.745 --> 00:26:37.958
In the US, they now say Ali was right.

00:26:38.018 --> 00:26:42.501
We were wrong about Vietnam.

00:26:42.561 --> 00:26:48.464
He fought for his people and for peace.

00:26:48.484 --> 00:26:52.934
He is our American Nelson Mandela.

00:26:52.994 --> 00:26:57.963
Ali gives a lot of money to the children of the world.

00:26:58.023 --> 00:27:00.693
He loves children.

00:27:00.754 --> 00:27:04.284
He always loves children.

00:27:04.345 --> 00:27:08.886
There are nine children in his family.

00:27:08.946 --> 00:27:13.146
He moves very slowly now.

00:27:13.206 --> 00:27:15.777
He sits at home.

00:27:15.837 --> 00:27:20.160
He gets tired very quickly.

00:27:20.221 --> 00:27:25.464
He likes watching his old fights on television.

00:27:25.524 --> 00:27:31.015
He is a good Muslim and a good man.

00:27:31.075 --> 00:27:35.766
People visit him and talk with him.

00:27:35.826 --> 00:27:42.197
Young Muhammad Ali talked and worked for black Americans.

00:27:42.257 --> 00:27:46.618
Then he was a famous boxing champion.

00:27:46.678 --> 00:27:51.039
But today they call him a people's champion.

